<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amarna archive</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akhetaten">Amarna</a> archive is the collection of clay tablets found at Amarna, the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akhenaten">Akhenaten</a>'s capital Akhetaten in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. It consists mainly of diplomatic letters in Akkadian between the Egyptian court and other rulers, including the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>. It is a key source for international relations in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age">Late Bronze Age</a> and for the Babylonian Empire's place in that system.</p></div>
